.TH SWAYKEYS 1 "2026-08-04" "swaykeys" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
swaykeys \- help sheet for every active sway key binding
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B swaykeys
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B swaykeys
parses the sway config the way sway itself does \(em following
.B include
directives, expanding
.B set
variables, tracking
.B mode
blocks \(em and prints every binding as a grouped, filterable help sheet.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-config " \fIPATH\fR"
Read this file instead of locating the running config. Disables the
IPC cross\-check.
.TP
.BR \-\-format " \fIFMT\fR"
Output format: \fBauto\fR, \fBplain\fR, \fBmd\fR or \fBjson\fR.
Default: auto.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print help and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print version and exit.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR sway (1),
.BR sway (5),
.BR sway-ipc (7)
